# LiveKit Voice AI Dashboard

A **self-hosted**, server-side rendered (SSR) dashboard for managing a private [LiveKit](https://livekit.io) server with AI voice agents, telephony, and real-time analytics. Built with **FastAPI** and **Jinja2** templates.

**Current Version:** v1.39.0

![Dashboard Overview](assets/dashboard-overview.png)

---

## ✨ Features

### 🎯 Core Dashboard
- **Real-Time Analytics** - Expandable sections for LiveKit, Telephony, Recording, Ingress, and Server Stats
- **Room Management** - List, create, close rooms; view participants and tracks
- **Live Session Cost** - Real-time cost tracking for active sessions
- **Network Quality** - RTT monitoring with color-coded quality indicators
- **Server Health** - CPU load, memory usage, disk space, and uptime tracking
- **AI Insights** - Aggregate analytics from call summaries:
  - Caller sentiment distribution (positive/neutral/negative)
  - Top conversation topics across all calls
  - LLM-analyzed call outcomes breakdown

### 🤖 AI Agent Management
- **Visual Agent Editor** - Configure LLM, STT, TTS, and voice settings via web UI
- **Realtime Pipeline Mode** - Single audio-to-audio stream for ultra-low latency with 5 providers (Google, Google Cloud, OpenAI, xAI, AWS)
  - Provider-aware advanced options: hidden when not supported by the selected provider
  - Google/Google Cloud: language, proactivity, affective dialog, thinking budget, context compression, top_p, max tokens
  - AWS: top_p and max_tokens support
- **Multi-Provider Support** - OpenAI, Anthropic, Google (Consumer + Vertex AI), Deepgram, ElevenLabs (TTS + STT), Cartesia, AWS Bedrock
- **Multi-Language Support** - 30+ languages for STT (Deepgram), 20+ languages for TTS (Google, Deepgram):
  - STT: English variants, Spanish, French, German, Portuguese, Italian, Dutch, Japanese, Korean, Chinese, Hindi, Arabic, Turkish, Nordic languages, and more
  - TTS: Language dropdown filters available voices; custom voice ID for unlisted languages
- **TTS Voice Dropdowns** - Pre-populated voice selectors for ElevenLabs, Cartesia, Deepgram (including Australian accents)
- **Multi-Agent Dispatch** - Route different phone numbers to different agents via dispatch rules
- **Conversation Dynamics** - VAD settings, Turn Detector, response delays, interrupt handling, end call on silence detection
- **Dynamic Endpointing** - Agent learns each caller's pause rhythm and adapts response timing automatically (livekit-agents 1.5.0)
- **Echo Cancellation Warmup** - Prevents phone echo from triggering false barge-ins at call start (configurable, default 3s)
- **False Interruption Recovery** - Agent resumes speech from where it left off after coughs, background noise, or brief acknowledgments
- **Turn Detection** - MultilingualModel v0.4.1-intl (39% fewer false interruptions, 14 languages)
- **Deepgram Flux Turn Detection** - Server-side turn detection with EOT threshold, timeout, and eager EOT options
- **Agent Handoffs** - Transfer calls between agents with two handoff types:
  - **Transfer** (Department Change) - Explicit handoff where the caller knows they're being transferred to a different agent/department
  - **Transition** (Multi-Prompt) - Seamless workflow phase change where the caller doesn't notice a switch
  - Sign-off prompt / bridge phrase, context modes (Full, Summary, Fresh), secondary greeting
- **Knowledge Base (RAG)** - Retrieval-Augmented Generation with vector search:
  - Create collections and upload documents (TXT, MD, CSV, PDF up to 10MB)
  - Add URL sources (web pages, Google Docs, Google Sheets) with auto-refresh intervals
  - Vector search with configurable chunk size, overlap, context expansion, and score threshold
  - Automatic text extraction from PDFs, re-indexing, and document download
  - Assign multiple collections per agent for real-time knowledge retrieval
- **Process Management** - Start/stop agents directly from dashboard
- **Export/Import v2.0** - Backup and restore agent configurations with handoff config and tool assignments
- **Prompt Versioning** - Automatic version history for system prompts with visual diff comparison, one-click restore, and configurable retention (5-50 versions per agent). API-initiated edits (via MCP) also create version entries tagged `source=mcp` with the calling API key's name recorded, so browser edits and programmatic edits share the same audit trail
- **AutoResearch** - AI-powered prompt optimization that analyzes real call transcripts to suggest improvements — manual or scheduled runs, reference call benchmarks, dual engine support (built-in OPRO + optional DSPy)
- **MCP / API Control** - External tools (Claude Code, Cursor, Claude Desktop, custom scripts) can manage every aspect of agents through the built-in Model Context Protocol server at `/mcp`. Full coverage of all ~150 agent configuration fields — prompt, voices, LLM/STT/TTS, realtime, conversation dynamics, voicemail/IVR detection, LLM fallback, knowledge-base assignments, extraction fields, handoffs, resource limits. API-key authenticated with IP allowlists and per-key rate limiting
- **Redis Caching** - 90% reduction in config file I/O with automatic fallback

### 📊 Call History
- **Call Tracking** - Automatic logging of all inbound/outbound calls
- **Transcription Viewer** - Color-coded speaker transcriptions with timestamps (collapsible)
- **Comprehensive Latency Monitoring** - Full round-trip latency tracking:
  - **Component Breakdown** - STT, LLM (TTFT), and TTS latency measured separately
  - **Percentile Tracking** - P50/P90/P99 metrics for performance analysis
  - **Visual Dashboard** - Doughnut chart for component distribution, trend line charts
  - **Per-Agent Analytics** - Compare latency performance across different agents
  - **Slow Call Detection** - Automatic flagging of calls with >1000ms latency
  - **Color-Coded Thresholds** - Green (<500ms), Yellow (500-1000ms), Red (>1000ms)
- **Live Latency on Active Calls** - Real-time TTFB display in Rooms page with auto-refresh
- **Filtering** - Filter by agent, direction, date range, phone number
- **Export** - Download call records as CSV or JSON (last 100/200/500/1000 or selected calls)
- **Bulk Delete** - Multi-select and delete multiple call records at once
- **Cloud Storage** - Sync call history to S3/GCS for permanent backup
- **Cloud Restore** - Restore call history from cloud storage to Redis
- **Storage Provider Selection** - Choose between local (Redis), S3, or GCS
- **AI-Powered Call Summary**:
  - LLM-generated summaries (OpenAI, Anthropic, Google)
  - **Key Topics** - Automatically extracted conversation topics as tags
  - **Call Outcome Badge** - Visual indicator (appointment booked, issue resolved, etc.)
  - **Action Items Checklist** - Follow-up tasks with interactive checkboxes
  - **Caller Sentiment Journey** - VADER-based sentiment sparkline showing emotional progression
  - **Interruption Analysis** - Track user vs agent interruptions
- **Call Recording Playback** - Play recordings directly from Call Detail page

### 🔧 Tools & Function Calling
- **Tool Registry** - Auto-discovery of tool files in `tools/` directory
- **Built-in Tools**:
  - **System**: Hangup, Hold, Blind Transfer, Attended Transfer (warm consultation)
  - **Communication**: SendSMS (HTTP API with auth options), SendEmail (SMTP/AWS SES)
  - **Utility**: GetDateTime, CollectDTMF (keypad/voice input), ScheduleCallback, RecordNote, PlayAudio, LookupCaller
- **Webhook Tools** - Custom HTTP integrations for n8n, make.com, Zapier:
  - Response handling with JSONPath extraction
  - Error handling with speak-on-error messages
  - Retry logic with configurable status codes and delays
  - Rate limiting (per-minute and per-session)
  - Authentication (bearer, basic, API key header/query)
  - Availability hours and condition expressions
  - Mock mode for testing without real HTTP calls
  - Execution logging for debugging
- **MCP Server Integration** - Connect Model Context Protocol servers for external AI tools:
  - Three transport types: SSE, Streamable HTTP, and Stdio (local subprocess via npx)
  - Pre-configured templates for Brave Search, GitHub, Filesystem, and Fetch servers
  - One-click sync to discover and cache available tools from connected servers
  - MCP tools assignable to agents alongside built-in and webhook tools
  - Automatic connection management with proper lifecycle cleanup
  - Environment variables and HTTP headers for server authentication
- **External Event Injection API** - Inject events into active calls from external systems
- **Per-Agent Assignment** - Assign specific tools to each agent
- **Max Tool Steps** - Configurable limit on consecutive tool calls per turn (default 3, increase for multi-step workflows)
- **Tool Configuration** - Schema-based configuration for each tool
- **Global Tool Configuration** - Configure built-in tools with API URLs, credentials, and settings via modal UI

### 📞 Telephony (SIP)
- **Inbound Trunks** - Dedicated page for inbound trunk management with export/import
- **Outbound Trunks** - Dedicated page for outbound calling with test call feature
- **Dispatch Rules** - Dedicated page for call routing with agent assignment and export/import
- **Phone Number Inventory** - Virtual aggregator showing all numbers across trunks
- **Outbound Campaigns** - Bulk calling system with CSV import, configurable concurrency, call pacing, scheduling, operating hours with timezone support, and real-time progress tracking
- **Navigation Shortcuts** - Quick links between telephony pages
- **Rule Statistics** - Total, direct, individual, and multi-line rule counts

### 🎥 Recording & Storage
- **Room Composite Recording** - Record entire rooms with layout options
- **Audio-Only Mode** - Works on 2 vCPU instances (recommended)
- **Recording Retention** - Configurable automatic cleanup of old recordings (1-365 days)
- **Cloud Storage** - Optional S3/GCS upload for recordings
- **Bulk Delete** - Multi-select and delete multiple recordings (local and cloud)
- **CPU Warning** - Automatic detection of hardware limitations
- **Proper Error Logging** - Full stack traces for debugging

### ⚙️ Settings & Configuration
- **API Key Management** - Store and manage AI provider keys with Test buttons to verify connections
- **API Test Buttons** - One-click testing for LLM (OpenAI, Anthropic, Google, xAI) and STT/TTS (Deepgram, ElevenLabs, Cartesia) API keys with latency display
- **System Resources** - Monitor/restart services, edit memory/CPU limits
- **System Logs** - View logs for all services (Dashboard, Agent, LiveKit, SIP, Egress)
- **Sub-User Management** - Create users with granular per-page permissions (view, create, edit, delete), monthly minutes quota, and hide technical details option
- **Permission Templates** - Read Only, Power User, Full Access, Customer Access presets
- **Route-Level Enforcement** - All routes enforce permissions; UI buttons hidden when user lacks permission
- **Customer Access** - Multi-tenant support with agent-based data filtering
- **Agent Assignment** - Assign specific agents to customer users for data isolation
- **Phone Number Assignment** - Assign specific phone numbers to customer users for view-only access
- **Call History Cloud Sync** - Sync call metadata to S3/GCS with restore capability
- **Audit Logging** - Track login/logout and user management actions
- **Two-Factor Authentication** - Optional TOTP-based 2FA
- **Forgot Password** - Email-based password reset with secure one-time links
- **Email Service** - Configure SMTP or AWS SES for dashboard emails (password resets, notifications)
- **Pricing & Cost Analytics** - Track per-call costs across LLM, STT, TTS, and realtime providers with margin support and currency conversion
- **Automated Reports** - Scheduled report generation with email delivery (daily, weekly, monthly)
- **Agent Simulation** - Automated testing of voice agents with configurable scenarios
- **Email Templates** - Customizable email templates with variable support and preview
- **Notes Tab** - Quick reference guides for Realtime models, Transfer & Transition handoffs, Turn Detector, STT models, and troubleshooting

### ❓ Contextual Help System
- **Page-Specific Help** - Click (?) button on any page for relevant documentation
- **Field Explanations** - Detailed descriptions of all configuration options
- **Section Guides** - Step-by-step explanations for each dashboard area

