## 🧠 AI Model Guide

Voice AI agents use three core components: **LLM** (reasoning), **STT** (speech-to-text), and **TTS** (text-to-speech), or a single **Realtime** audio-to-audio stream. Choosing the right combination affects latency, quality, and cost.

### LLM Models (Large Language Models)

| Provider | Model | Latency (TTFT) | Quality | Cost | Best For |
|----------|-------|----------------|---------|------|----------|
| **OpenAI** | GPT-4o | 300-500ms | Excellent | $$ | Balanced quality/speed, general purpose |
| | GPT-4o Mini | 200-300ms | Good | $ | Budget-friendly, simpler conversations |
| | GPT-4.1 | 300-400ms | Excellent | $$ | Smarter than 4o, better reasoning |
| | GPT-4.1 Mini | 150-250ms | Good | $ | Fast responses, good quality |
| | GPT-4.1 Nano | 100-200ms | Basic | $ | Cheapest, simple Q&A |
| | GPT-5.1 Instant | 200-350ms | Excellent | $$ | Latest reasoning model, instant mode |
| | GPT-5.2 Instant | 250-400ms | Best | $$$ | Smartest OpenAI model, complex tasks |
| **Google** | Gemini 2.5 Flash | 150-300ms | Excellent | $ | Fast, cost-effective, great quality |
| | Gemini 3 Flash Preview | 150-300ms | Best | $ | Latest model, best Google quality |
| **Anthropic** | Claude Haiku 4.5 | 200-350ms | Good | $ | Fast, affordable Claude |
| | Claude Sonnet 5 | 300-500ms | Excellent | $$ | Best Claude for voice, nuanced |
| **AWS Bedrock** | Claude Haiku 4.5 (AU) | 250-400ms | Good | $ | Data stays in Australia |
| | Claude Sonnet 4.5 (AU) | 350-550ms | Excellent | $$ | Australian data residency |
| | Amazon Nova Micro | 100-200ms | Basic | $ | Fastest AWS option, simple tasks |
| | Amazon Nova Pro | 200-350ms | Good | $ | Better quality Nova model |
| **xAI** | Grok-4 Fast | 150-300ms | Good | $$ | Fast, conversational |
| | Grok-4.1 Fast | 150-300ms | Excellent | $$ | Newest Grok, improved quality |

### STT Models (Speech-to-Text)

| Provider | Model | Latency | Accuracy | Languages | Best For |
|----------|-------|---------|----------|-----------|----------|
| **Deepgram** ⭐ | Flux (Low Latency) | ~100ms | Good | English | **Best for real-time voice AI** - fastest |
| | Nova 3 | ~150ms | Excellent | 36+ | Best accuracy, multilingual |
| | Nova 2 | ~200ms | Good | 36+ | Stable, proven model |
| **OpenAI** | Whisper v1 | 500-1000ms | Excellent | 99+ | Non-realtime, post-processing |
| | GPT-4o Transcribe | 300-500ms | Best | 50+ | Highest accuracy, context-aware |
| | GPT-4o Mini Transcribe | 200-400ms | Excellent | 50+ | Faster, still very accurate |
| **Google** | Chirp 3 | 200-400ms | Excellent | 125+ | Best multilingual support |
| | Chirp 2 | 200-400ms | Good | 125+ | Stable, many languages |
| **ElevenLabs** | Scribe v2 Realtime | ~150ms | Excellent | 32 | Fast, good for voice AI |
| **AWS** | Transcribe Streaming | 200-400ms | Good | 50+ | AWS integration, data residency |

### TTS Models (Text-to-Speech)

| Provider | Model | Latency (TTFB) | Quality | Best For |
|----------|-------|----------------|---------|----------|
| **ElevenLabs** ⭐ | Flash v2.5 | ~75ms | Excellent | **Best for voice AI** - fastest + natural |
| | Turbo v2.5 | ~250ms | Best | Highest quality, slightly slower |
| **Cartesia** | Sonic 2 (2024-11) | ~50ms | Good | Fastest TTS available |
| | Sonic 3 (2025-01) | ~50ms | Excellent | Fastest + improved quality |
| **Deepgram** | Aura-2 Voices | ~100ms | Good | Multi-language (EN, ES, FR, DE, IT, NL, JA) |
| **OpenAI** | TTS-1 | ~200ms | Good | Budget option, adequate quality |
| | TTS-1 HD | ~300ms | Excellent | Best OpenAI quality |
| | GPT-4o Mini TTS | ~200ms | Excellent | Newest, expressive voices |
| **Google** | Neural2 / Wavenet | ~250ms | Good | Many accents (US, AU, GB, IN) |
| | Chirp 3 HD | ~200ms | Excellent | Latest Google voices, multilingual |

### Recommended Configurations

| Scenario | LLM | STT | TTS | Total Latency |
|----------|-----|-----|-----|---------------|
| **⚡ Lowest Latency** | GPT-4.1 Mini or Gemini 2.5 Flash | Deepgram Flux | Cartesia Sonic 3 or ElevenLabs Flash | ~350-500ms |
| **🏆 Best Quality** | GPT-5.2 Instant or Claude Sonnet 5 | Deepgram Flux | ElevenLabs Turbo v2.5 | ~500-700ms |
| **⚖️ Best Balance** | GPT-4o or Gemini 2.5 Flash | Deepgram Nova 3 | ElevenLabs Flash v2.5 | ~450-650ms |
| **💰 Budget Friendly** | GPT-4o Mini or GPT-4.1 Nano | Deepgram Nova 2 | Deepgram Aura-2 or OpenAI TTS-1 | ~400-600ms |

### Realtime Models (Audio-to-Audio)

Realtime providers use a single audio-to-audio stream, combining STT, LLM, and TTS in one connection for ultra-low latency.

| Provider | Models | Voices | Latency | Key Features | API Key |
|----------|--------|--------|---------|--------------|---------|
| **Google** ⭐ | Gemini 2.5 Flash Native Audio | Puck, Charon, Kore, Fenrir, Aoede + more | <200ms | Language, proactivity, affective dialog, thinking budget, context compression | `GOOGLE_API_KEY` |
| **Google Cloud** | Gemini 2.5 Flash Native Audio | Same as Google | <200ms | Same as Google, enterprise Vertex AI integration | Service Account |
| **OpenAI** | GPT-4o Realtime | alloy, echo, ash, ballad, coral, sage + more | ~300ms | Playback speed, turn detection, noise reduction, modalities | `OPENAI_API_KEY` |
| **xAI** | Grok 2 Realtime | Ara, Rex, Sal, Eve, Leo | ~300ms | Playback speed, turn detection, noise reduction | `XAI_API_KEY` |
| **AWS** | Amazon Nova 2 Sonic | tiffany, matthew, amy + more | ~300ms | AWS integration, top_p, max_tokens, turn detection sensitivity | AWS Credentials |

### Tips for Low Latency

1. **Use streaming models** - All recommended STT/TTS models support streaming for faster response
2. **Keep prompts concise** - Shorter system prompts = faster LLM processing
3. **Regional routing** - Use Bedrock AU/APAC if your users are in Australia/Asia
4. **Responsiveness slider** - Higher values (0.7-0.9) make the agent respond faster but may cut off users
5. **Choose the right quality level** - Not every use case needs the smartest model
6. **Try Realtime mode** - Google Gemini Live offers <200ms latency with a single audio-to-audio stream

