## 📖 Usage Guide

### Overview Page (`/`)

Expandable sections showing:
- **Live Sessions** - Active rooms with cost tracking
- **Recording & Storage** - Active recordings, success rate, storage used
- **Telephony** - SIP trunk status, call volume
- **Server Stats** - CPU, memory, disk, uptime

### Call History (`/call-history`)

- **Call Records** - View all inbound/outbound calls with filtering
- **Transcriptions** - Color-coded speaker transcripts
- **Metrics** - Duration, TTFB latency, end reason
- **Export** - Download as CSV or JSON

### Tools (`/tools`)

- **Tool Registry** - View all available tools (built-in, webhook, and MCP)
- **Webhook Tools** - Create custom HTTP integrations
- **MCP Servers** - Connect MCP servers for external AI tools (web search, GitHub, etc.)
- **Agent Assignment** - Assign tools to specific agents

### Agents (`/agents`)

- **Create/Edit Agents** - Full visual editor for all settings
- **Multi-Agent Dispatch** - Route calls to different agents
- **Start/Stop** - Control agent processes directly
- **Export/Import** - Backup configurations as JSON

### Recording & Storage (`/egress`)

- **Start Recording** - Select room, layout, audio/video options
- **CPU Warning** - Banner shows if hardware is limited
- **Audio-Only Recommended** - Works on 2 vCPU instances

> ⚠️ **Hardware Note:** Video recording requires 4 vCPU. Audio-only works on 2 vCPU.

### Settings (`/settings`)

**Tabs:**
- **General** - Server info, connection status
- **Integrations/API** - API keys for AI providers with Test buttons to verify connections (requires `settings.edit` permission to modify)
- **Security** - Password change, 2FA setup
- **User Management** - Sub-users with granular permissions (main admin only)
- **Dependencies** - Install/update packages, view LiveKit plugins (requires `settings.edit` for changes)
- **System Resources** - Monitor/restart services, edit limits (requires `settings.edit` for changes)
- **System Logs** - View service logs (requires `settings.view` permission)
- **Notes** - Quick reference guides

**Permission Notes:** Sub-users with `settings.view` can see settings but cannot modify them. The `settings.edit` permission is required to change API keys, install packages, restart services, or modify resource limits.

